    "result_text": "Done. All changes are in place and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`). The runtime audit line confirms the behaviour end-to-end:\n\n```\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"memberId\":\"NSWV227169701686\",\n         \"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n## What changed (6 files, each edit small and local)\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** \u2014 the `V2` tag is mixed into each identifier's input, so every value differs from v1 and no v1 value can recur:\n- `HouseholdId.java` \u2014 hash input prefixed with `\"V2|\"`.\n- `IdentityKey.java` \u2014 hash input prefixed with `\"V2|\"`.\n- `AssignCustomerCode.java` (memberId) \u2014 region code inside the identifier is now the plain region plus the `V2` tag (`NSWV2\u2026`), and the hash input is prefixed with `\"V2|\"`.\n\nBecause these three helpers are the single source of truth, every consumer (uniqueness checks, household ceiling, membership, possible-duplicate) stays internally consistent without edits.\n\n**Non-identifier fields left as plain region** \u2014 `locality`, `timezone`, and `OwnerSegment`'s derived region all still call `Locality.of(...)` directly, so `locality` stays `'NSW'` and the `V2` tag never leaks into them.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2.\n- Added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema and a nested `identity` object holding `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`; removed those three from the top level. A small static `OwnerMapper.identity(owner)` builds the block.\n\n**Audit event** (`LogAuditOnCreate.java`) \u2014 the structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` moved to schema version 2: added `\"schemaVersion\":2` and the recomputed `ownerSegment`; its `memberId` is the v2 identity.\n\nThe request/input fields (`OwnerFields`) are unchanged.\n\nStructural cost was kept low: each edited method is a small single-purpose function (low `WMC_other`), edits are 1\u20133 lines each, and the only new method is a tiny DTO builder.",
