    "probe_text": "I've traced the entire pipeline. Here is the ordered list of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the endpoint file requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; without that role the request never enters the pipeline.\n- The whole pipeline runs under a single `transaction` governance, committing once at the end.\n\n## Steps in order\n\nEach step below is either a **validation** (can reject and short-circuit) or a **side-effect** (mutates state, persists, or logs). Steps 2\u20137 all read/mutate the request body (`OwnerFieldsDto`); step 10 onward work on the built `Owner` entity.\n\n1. **CheckIdempotency** *(side-effect / short-circuit)* \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was sent and is already known, it loads the previously-created owner and responds **200**, skipping the entire create. Otherwise it takes the `proceed` branch.\n\n2. **ValidateOwnerFields** *(validation)* \u2014 binds the `@RequestBody` and rejects with **400** (`MissingFieldsException`) if any required field is blank: `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and address (needs either `addressLine1` or `address`). This is the only step that reads the body.\n\n3. **ValidatePostcode** *(validation)* \u2014 if a postcode is present it must be 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in that range; otherwise **400**. Absent postcode passes.\n\n4. **NormalizeTelephone** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 rewrites telephone to E.164 (`+61` assumed, strips separators, drops a leading `0`), then validates national-number length (+61\u21929 digits, +1\u219210) and total 8\u201315 digits; bad number \u2192 **400**. Stores the normalized value back on the request.\n\n5. **NormalizeEmail** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 if email present, must match the email regex (else **400**); lower-cases it and stores it back. Absent/blank email passes.\n\n6. **RejectDisposableEmail** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects with **400** if the email domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Absent/blank email passes.\n\n7. **NormalizeAddress** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; composes `address` from line1(+line2) and writes it (and the lines) back. If the result is blank \u2192 **400**.\n\n8. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** *(validation)* \u2014 computes an `IdentityKey` (SHA-256 over normalized telephone + lower-cased email + Soundex of last name) and scans all non-deleted owners; a match is a **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`).\n\n9. **EnsureCityCapacity** *(validation)* \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); at **50 or more** it rejects with **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n\n10. **BuildOwner** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 maps the request to an `Owner` entity. A `registrationDate` in the future is a **400**; otherwise defaults to today, then rolls forward off weekends/public holidays via `BusinessDay.roll`.\n\n11. **EnsureDailyLimit** *(validation)* \u2014 counts existing owners already carrying the new owner's (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`; at **100 or more** it rejects with **429** (`DailyLimitExceededException`).\n\n12. **AssignCustomerCode** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>V2` + 2-digit fiscal year + 8-hex-char SHA-256 of (`V2|`+telephone+lastName) + a Luhn check digit.\n\n13. **DeduplicateCustomerCode** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if that code collides with an existing owner's `customerCode`, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique.\n\n14. **AssignNamesakeCount** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` to the number of existing owners whose first+last name match (case-insensitive).\n\n15. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n16. **RecordIdempotency** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records key\u2192new owner id so a repeat returns this owner.\n\n17. **LogAuditOnCreate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` log line and a structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON (schemaVersion 2, memberId, membership level, owner segment), plus a `NOTIFY` \"welcome\" line.\n\n18. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect / response)* \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, decorates it with computed (non-persisted) fields \u2014 `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, possible-duplicate mark, membership mark, risk flag \u2014 and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Notes\n- Validations run **before** the entity is built and saved, so an invalid request never persists.\n- Steps 8, 9, 11, 13, 14 each call `ownerRepository.findAll()` \u2014 the uniqueness/capacity/count checks are computed in-application over all owners, not via DB constraints.\n- The decorations in step 18 (`bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, etc.) affect only the response DTO, not what was stored."
